h(1, 900, """A secure peace is not a strategic alliance. It will be a secure truce, even if the masses think it an era of comprehensive peace!""")

t(1, 1520, """“Reproach is in proportion to love” is a deviant, satanic phrase that brings about dispute and quarrelling among people, and it is a clear contradiction of the noble Prophetic guidance! You will not find two who reproached each other and then returned to their first state of love and affection, unless they are in a strong bond of love above every dispute, and this is realised in one or two people in the life of each of us, not in all the people in our lives.

The Mother of the Believers Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, says: "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never took revenge for himself in anything, unless a sanctity of Allah was violated."

And from the testimony of the Prophet's servant Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him: Anas said: "I served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years, and he never said 'uff' to me, nor did he say of something I did: Why did you do it? Nor of something I left: Why did you leave it?"

Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal says: "Nine tenths of good character lies in overlooking.”""")

h(1, 2300, """The most worthless phrase in folk heritage: Reproach is in proportion to love!""")

t(2, 345, """The one wronged all his life, who wept all the years of his life, and who was transgressed against throughout the course of his life, may think that revenge is the best solution toward the oppressor who ruined his world for him. He does not know that forgiveness is nobility of character and a uniting of hearts to support the truth on earth in realising the Divine project, which is more important than personal revenge. In forgiveness there is a practical belittling of the worth of the world, which has no value, in the eyes of all people. It also pushes the oppressor toward a new life in which he will live with constant pangs of conscience, and he will not escape his conscience however he tries, because the matter is not in his hands; and even if that does not apply to all who are forgiven, it shows in many of them. Revenge for the harm of the years, the pain of a lifetime and the agonies of time is through forgiveness, not through severity and holding to account. Whoever said "Reproach is in proportion to love" has gone astray, for the oppressor lives his whole life believing it is his right to practise oppression. So whom will you reproach? Will you reproach someone who believes you are his slave, that Allah created you to worship him instead of Allah?

Do not reproach those from whom came the hideous, horrific oppression that you swallowed through the years of your lives; forgive and pardon as much as you can, for a whole life lost to oppression, reproach as a reaction does not bring back the years that were lost in grief, weeping and sorrow. As for punishment, it will relieve the oppressor, and he will feel that he no longer owes the wronged one any right. The wronged one who is given power on earth, when Allah the Exalted enables him with the means of retribution, has a right and rights; if he takes retribution, the oppressor is relieved, and the oppressor does not deserve to be relieved!""")

h(2, 1150, """“Go, for you are free”: A great nobility of character, and a hard crisis of conscience for those pardoned!""")

h(2, 2100, """In public, governmental work: Every excessive reassurance in it is a door to a possible fall and catastrophe!""")

t(3, 95, """🟢 Accumulations of 7 or 8 or 9 years of peace on the surface, and of many hidden conflicts in the depth!
🟢 A harsh discourse containing the might of Islam and the dominance of Islam "as the single global power", and what that means for a party accustomed to doing the same thing in the days of its strength!
🟢 Stern, swift and decisive decisions whose spirit is command and prohibition, not requesting and begging, and in them is a pride that Allah loves, because it is pride in displaying the might of the religion and its people.""")

h(3, 650, """*The Great Malhama* — The only war in which there is difficulty; it is the product of a harsh discourse, and the product of decisions that fear none but Allah!""")

t(3, 1210, """Abu Jahl, Abu Lahab, al-Walid and others .. they practised oppression as a way .. Every soul that sees the light is a soul whose way is not oppression!""")

h(3, 1600, """Oppression, oppression, oppression .. Oppression, oppression, oppression .. Oppression, oppression — The cause of the intensifying blindness of insight despite witnessing the overwhelming signs!""")

t(3, 2115, """Oppression brings down the wrath of the Mighty Lord, so He punishes the oppressor by sealing over his heart .. I ask Allah the Mighty for guidance for every Muslim man and woman .. The Muslim must always watch over his conduct""")

h(3, 2400, """Oppression, oppression .. Oppression, oppression — The cause of blindness of insight!""")

t(4, 570, """A new generation of the sons of the Arabs, from all countries without exception, is today breaking this long-lasting state in which previous generations drowned

99% of the lack of organisation and of the randomness in managing work at the world level is found in the Arab world, and there are considerable differences among the Arab peoples: some are the most random, and some are less random. As for the remaining 1% of randomness in managing work in the world, it is distributed over the rest of the world's population!""")

h(4, 1100, """90% of work problems in any sector are caused by the one who manages being a disorganised person!""")

t(4, 1700, """What hinders the development of Muslims among the nations. I ask Allah the Mighty that this post contributes to enlightening the minds of those who need it. How many conflicts people have put before me over the years, and they still come to me in their consultations; perhaps these words are a cure for those kinds of conflicts, if Allah the Exalted wills.

The post

Do not chase mouths, for they do not harm. How many people wasted their lives and spent their youth chasing what so-and-so said about them and the comments of such-and-such about them: this one insulted him, that one described him with evil, another threw at him what is in himself, and others and others and others. The one in error about himself did not realise that a great mass of people are trivial; they live trivial and – Allah knows best – die trivial. And what does the trivial one do with his time? He talks and talks.. And what will he talk about while he is trivial? He will talk with the smallest of words and phrases, and the smallest of small talk he says about people: backbiting! There is nothing smaller than backbiting and living in this world only to mention so-and-so and such-and-such a woman with evil. Those exposed to this evil are in the millions, and they are almost 99% of humans. The post is not about backbiting, but about those who have taken the project of the Hereafter seriously and taken hold of the Book of Allah with strength; if these busy themselves with mouths, their lives will be ruined, and they will lose much and much in this world and the Hereafter. So fear Allah in yourselves, and free yourselves from the shackles of mouths, for chasing mouths is a clear loss; they are losing mouths in losing bodies, trying to drag others into the loss they are in. The Muslim man and woman must be aware, wise and astute, because the snare of mouths and its net are a trap for life, a trap for worship, a trap for self-development, and a trap that hinders knowing Allah the Exalted. Millions of people in every age and land lived and died drowning in gossip, backbiting and talebearing; they lived small and died small, and they are the ones who did that to themselves, and they became corpses in graves and offered nothing of benefit to themselves or to humanity. They are the model of evil and the people of evil. Do not waste your project of the Hereafter, for which you were created, by chasing their mouths; the disease has spread, the malady has worsened, the affliction has become general, and the cure has become impossible""")

h(5, 350, """One of the greatest losses: Chasing people's mouths!""")

t(5, 845, """How do you translate this into an understanding followed by conduct?
Do not fear people saying of you: poor
Do not fear people saying of you: a failure
Do not fear people saying of you: a lying charlatan

Do not fear people saying anything of you that upsets you, because every right and true conduct you will do built on the rule: "What will people say about me?" is conduct that will certainly be wrong, not possibly.

You commit the error because you do not want your self to blame you, and you do not want people to blame you even if your self is in error and the people are in error; yet you say: I do not want anyone to find me wrong, even if I will commit the error with everyone!

Your true servitude to Allah the Exalted starts from this rule, and you are tested in this matter every day. My words do not mean that you clash with the family and society, because there are dozens of issues in our lives that are not confrontational, and not every issue we clash over actually deserves that we clash over it; we must classify issues, sort and sift them, and live with wisdom, not impulsiveness.

As for the issues of worship and tawhid, there is no laxity in them, and certain, confirmed oppression by which the five necessities, or one of them, are harmed also accepts no laxity. But I say as advice: classify, and do not mix everything in one basket. Not every disagreement of conscience deserves the destruction of a family or the severing of family ties.

Returning to the root of the post: in everything that does not harm you or others, the door is open for you to do what is fully right, and you are not excused for not doing what is fully right in it.

Preparation for the future is first through this intellectual building, which will be followed by posts, if Allah wills, to explain other elements in it .. then by teaching it to the wife if possible, and among the wives, teaching it to the husband if possible .. Put a thousand lines under "if possible"! It is not right for a family to be destroyed over intellectual disagreements .. The only Guide is our Mighty Lord alone .. But if spreading this intellectual building is possible, that is good, and if it is not possible, the fixed rule is: "To you your religion and to me mine" .. Beware of destroying yourselves with grief over anyone, for every adult, sane grown-up carries the thought he wants .. And I say the children are always more deserving of every effort ..

Starting from the first thing in the post, building a person's thought on not fearing the world becomes the greatest entrance to fixing certainty in the heart, and it is exactly what came in yesterday's comments: How do we prepare for the exceptional future to come, which no past age or time in the history of humanity resembles?

If you were told that your coming days will be on the pavement, and you smiled with all strength, courage and contentment, then you have built the rule of not fearing the world.

If you were told that next year your food will be only bread, and you smiled with all strength, courage and contentment, then you have built the rule of not fearing the world

If you were told that for ten years you will have no fixed, stable provision, and you smiled with all strength, courage and contentment, then you have built the rule of not fearing the world

If you were told that everything by which people's lives are kept upright, the basics such as housing, food and continuous provision, will not be given to you for a year or for ten, and you were not shaken, did not fear, did not grieve, but rather considered that strength and not weakness, then you have crossed a bridge on one side of which stand the people, and on the other side stand the prophets and those who walked their path.

Preparation for the coming future, with its abundance of wealth and the great riches in it, is a preparation for cleansing the heart, so that the one who prepares and is ready for what is coming is not tempted. From the severity of the ignorance of those who spoke during the past years, people were not told the truth about the future .. The truth that was hidden from people is that what is coming is a blessing and riches whose like people have never seen .. While the speakers themselves memorised nothing of what is coming but wars and malahim, so they led themselves astray and led people astray, and went on telling people: Prepare for the malahim, which are only the Great Malhama""")

t(6, 65, """and turned it into malahim, and ignored, out of ignorance, the truth of continuous years of comfortable living with abundant wealth and blessing without malahim or wars. Neither did they themselves understand, nor did the people they spoke to understand, the truth of the coming trial of the world, because they basically did not know it and learned nothing about it, and if they knew it, they did not pay attention and did not reflect!

Preparation for what is coming is preparation to strengthen and reinforce the bond with Allah the Exalted, because what is coming at the level of wealth, riches, blessing, abundance and great good, by the leave of the Mighty Provider, is a very, very great trial that has no like and has never had a like in the history of the Ummah.""")

h(6, 650, """The greatest preparation for the future is through not fearing the world""")

t(6, 1210, """What is coming is not merely a cycle of history .. What is coming is a revolution in all of history .. What is coming is of a new era whose outward appearance is riches, wealth and comfortable living, then malahim, and yet the matter is other than all this ..

By what is coming I do not mean here comfortable living, nor the malahim, nor anything related to the world, for all this is known to people .. What is coming that I want attention paid to reflecting on the greatness of what is in it is that what is coming is a door that has not been opened since Adam, peace be upon him .. This door is being knocked by the hand of "the miniature image" of the moon of Banu Hashim, upon him and his family be blessings and peace.

We must remember that this door, which was never knocked before in the history of humanity, is a door that when it opens will move humanity to a short station; so preparing for it requires understanding its context and grasping its truth and its outcomes!

Opening the door of the major signs does not require turning to monasticism and turning away from the responsibilities of life, but it requires planning for the final years, since they will be the last years of the earth for this Ummah, and this will require many of the necessities of exceptional understanding and comprehension, since the whole matter is exceptional and utterly unique; what is coming has absolutely no likeness to anything humans have lived since Adam, peace be upon him!

The journey of humanity will then have reached the station of final departure .. and souls deserve full understanding, not a part or parts of the truth.""")

h(6, 2150, """What is coming is not of the simplicity common in understandings. What is coming is a matter that has had no like since Adam, peace be upon him""")


t(7, 155, """Have you ever heard of a prophet who imitated his people? Have you ever heard of a reformer who imitated others? So, through the opposite of what people are used to, through other than a wrong custom that has fermented in their souls, and through what is hard for souls to do, the qualities of being chosen become clear; except for a clear, unbearable oppression, or a crime about which silence is a crime. Beyond that, the chosen have no share in it but imitating the morals of prophethood, and they walk on the path of the prophets imitating them in conduct.""")

h(7, 650, """Through the opposite of the customary, the qualities of being chosen become clear!""")

t(7, 1195, """Just yesterday.. only 100 years separate us from the sacrifices of our grandfathers and grandmothers!

O young man who no longer sees any value in his life, whom frustration has wrapped and crushed.. those bloods, the bloods of your grandfathers, were shed without condition or limit, for your sake! They were shed so that you would live with your head held high, even if a thousand thousand storms besieged you!

O girl who no longer sees any value in her life.. the burden your grandmothers carried when the horses returned empty of their riders was a heavy burden, heavier than death itself; your grandmothers raised the children and were mother and father, so that you would be born after 50 and 100 years to live as free women with heads held high, not for the world to make you its captives, its morsels, its fallen ones and its base ones!""")

h(7, 1900, """Our grandfathers watered the land with their blood, and our grandmothers carried the burden!""")

t(7, 2410, """Balfour died .. Moshe died .. Picot died .. Balfour left daughters behind .. Dayan left daughters behind .. Rise, O screams from beneath the soil .. Rise and speak, for the day of your revenge has come, for the world will hear you in spite of itself .. O screams buried in Deir Yassin .. in Sabra and in Shatila .. in Saydnaya .. in Abu Ghraib .. in Setif, Guelma and Kherrata .. in Denshawai .. and in Manshiya of Libya""")

h(8, 350, """The rifle has appeared, and the lion is about to appear""")

t(8, 910, """And the orphans, the bereaved and the widows will soon, if Allah wills, have a father.. The cage will not stay alive.. The shackles will die of helplessness.. The eyes of the locks will melt in terror.. The arrogance of the bars will be humbled in disgrace, and the watching crowds will shake in fear after living their lifetime watching with laughter.. mockery.. and gloating!""")

h(8, 1350, """The lion is close to leaving the cage""")

t(8, 1885, """We may differ in experiences, in views, in understandings, in interests and in orientations, and each of us may be from a world that does not resemble the other's world; yet all this does not necessarily have to be a barrier or an obstacle ever before affection for Allah the Exalted, when souls gather on the pleasure of Allah the Exalted. For a group of opposites and mutually averse people in views, understanding, experience, perception and orientation is still able to gather for Allah the Exalted within the bounds of reform on earth, and not necessarily within the bounds of mutual affection, familiarity, love and closeness. These are provisions among people that Allah the Exalted perhaps did not write, for a profound wisdom that none knows but He, Whose every name is sanctified. So every relationship whose spirit is respect is a relationship that continues for Allah the Exalted, even if hearts differ, understandings are averse, views are opposed and orientations clash, and this happens when people gather on a comprehensive matter in which there is good and reform.""")

h(8, 2400, """The most beautiful thing between opposites is that Allah the Exalted brings them together""")

t(9, 585, """In each there is good, and both of them are reformers on earth""")

h(9, 900, """Affection between people: an affection of love, and an affection of noble character""")

t(9, 1475, """Strange are fathers whose wives became many and whose offspring scattered, and then the mutual aversion of the children astonishes them! It is no wonder that they descend from one loins (one father) and their hearts are divided; if this is the discord between the sons of one man, then how far apart are the souls of strangers!""")

h(9, 1950, """Moving a mountain is easier than bringing one person close to another!""")

t(9, 2485, """A person should not exhaust himself, his spirit, his mind, his clarity of thought and his psychological ease to make someone love someone .. Love is impossible and inconceivable to bring about by means .. My experience is varied, of many scenes and very deep, and what I say is the essence of the experiences of what I have seen in people of different dispositions!""")

t(10, 95, """Bringing opposites together is ruin for people and corruption of their states. Hearts, love, closeness, psychological fusion and everything resembling these terms do not come by a human act based on means, however great they are; rather, this matter is exclusively and specifically among what Allah the Exalted has reserved for Himself. Bringing people together, especially if they are "in intellectual, mental and psychological opposition", is a righteous deed, but one should not insist on it when the forms of opposition are plain, clear and unambiguous; for minds, souls and spirits all fuse only by a pure Divine will, and the fusion between individuals of one world and individuals of another world is something we almost find no evidence of happening throughout history.""")

h(10, 650, """Love is guidance of the heart, and hearts are of the command of Allah!""")

t(10, 1245, """If accepting kindness is a cause of the impossibility of lifting an oppression realised on earth, it is forbidden for the Muslim to accept it""")

h(10, 1650, """Justice is a sword that kindness breaks!""")

t(10, 2130, """Wherever you find them, they are the people with whom whoever knows them is not wretched, and all of them on earth are servants of the purposes of Allah, not of anyone of His creation""")

h(10, 2400, """The doer of good for Allah: by him justice is upheld, not against him""")

t(11, 590, """If Allah the Exalted wills.. it is glad tidings for every wronged man and every wronged woman.. and for everyone who chose the path to Allah the Exalted through hardship, toil, exhaustion and patience, and did not deviate.""")

h(11, 1000, """Blessed is everyone who saw true visions and knew that his appointed time is not near, and that he is going on to the soundness of self and religion""")

t(11, 1535, """Work for today, because it may be the last day! Man has no future! Where did the concept of the future come from?! How can there be a future when a person (any of us) may die in less than half a minute from now?! Work for today.. for this day of yours.. for you cannot guarantee tomorrow at all! How many will die today, and they will say of him: He intended to do such and such tomorrow?! He was intending.. He intended, but the hour of his death does not care for what he wanted.. Intend what you wish, you are free.. but the decision is in the heavens, not with you!""")

h(11, 2050, """The world is stations, and every one of its stations is a last one!""")

t(12, 95, """In 2022 I published an old video in which I said: there is no faster road to Allah the Exalted than the road of justice, and no faster road to Satan than the road of oppression!""")

h(12, 450, """When oppression occurs, the echo of the grievance does not stop until it is lifted""")

h(12, 1350, """Establishing justice and supporting the oppressed cannot be done without the soul being free of the unease by which the will to speak and to act is bridled!""")

t(12, 1905, """Praise be to Allah, Who saved us from believing in matter, in money, in status and in means as being what is relied and depended upon, that by them the back is strengthened and the matter stands, and that on them one leans in times of calamity. May Allah protect us, you and our offspring from believing in the loftiness of means, for Allah is the Lord, and whoever knows the meaning of the Lord knows everything!""")

h(12, 2300, """The world is not, and will not be, 1+1=2""")

h(13, 700, """Reform on earth: Reliance on the King, astuteness, intelligence, wisdom, vision, will, planning, stratagem, politics, forbearance and courage""")

t(13, 1300, """The role of the true reforming person on earth begins with his understanding of right and wrong, then with his moving to the stage of empowerment on earth to carry out his reform structure on which he was built for years!

Two successive, inseparable steps; one should not precede the other, it is not permissible for one to be preferred over the other, and it is not right for one to suffice itself without the other!""")

h(13, 1850, """The poor are not fed, clothed or made to live with dignity by philosophical theorising! The philosophy of understanding right and wrong is an engine for the mind, and it is not bread given to the poor, nor a house and money granted to him!""")

t(13, 2365, """The greatest wonder of all is a mufti who gives fatwas according to his own body's particular urges and according to his intellectual thinking and his particular self, and generalises his own body's particular urges, the urges of his self and the urges of the particularity of his make-up onto all people. Among the men of the pulpits there is one who loves polygamy with a great love and talks to people, but he does not stop as the upright one stops for his prayer at the rulings of the religion and at the rights of women, which are at the highest level of strictness, nor stop at the fine details of them in the law of our Mighty Lord. Another talks to people and gives them fatwas, and finds in himself nothing but deep-rooted urges of a self that inclines to the one wife who is never given a second, for that is how his self was created, so he says to people:""")

t(14, 55, """Be sensible and wise, and beware of polygamy, and do not be mad!

I am not speaking here as a supporter or an opponent, and in my post I am never addressing my sisters among women or my brothers among men. This post is directed at the shaykhs, the preachers and the Islamic thinkers on the pulpits, so I will not reply to a supporter or an opponent. This post is not about the topic of polygamy. This post is directed at those who give fatwas from the two camps: the camp of laxity and neglect, and the camp of prohibiting and forbidding out of dislike; the post is for them, not for women and men.

The one who speaks to people as a preacher and encourages polygamy in his answers to a questioner, without strictly warning about the rights of women as part of fulfilling the trust of knowledge and exhortation, is in error. And the one who takes multiple wives while unable to clear his account before Allah the Mighty on the Day of Resurrection in achieving the "non-heartfelt" justice is not excused by his ignorance; he must gain understanding and learn, and that is the role of courts and laws before it is the role of mosques. This one too is in error, walking among the doubts of committing the certain, forbidden oppression on earth; unless he was overtaken, and the means swept him up and down without an intention of oppression, so he did not premeditate, and took multiple wives without knowing what his fates would carry for him in his coming years from the unseen hidden from every person; that is another matter.

As for the one whom Allah created content with one woman, and who was given a pulpit, stood on it and said to all Muslim men: Come to your senses, O madmen, and be sensible; his words have nothing to do with reason, for fatwa is not like this, and the thinker does not look at the issues of society like this, because society is not a representation of the person of the one speaking on the pulpit. The one I criticise, I criticise for what I heard from him today in an old sermon on polygamy when he lived in Europe; he was presented to the Islamic world as a very great Islamic thinker, and I am never against a person being described with what befits his thought, this touches nothing in myself at all, but I am amazed at the number of intellectual slips!

For this reason it is not right to steer the social helm of society from a corrupt perspective at the level of assessing the needs of society. If Allah the Exalted created me content with one wife, that is a beautiful thing, because every nature is a beautiful thing. But if today I do not love something, and that is how I was formed in my own particular nature, not loving it, then how do I accuse others in society of madness and lack of wisdom?!

The talk is not about polygamy. I will not comment on an attack that comes very often from our sisters among women. I am speaking here exclusively and specifically with those who stand on the pulpit and address the public consciousness: Rulings cannot be confined to the context of one self! You as a speaker and the holder of a pulpit are one person and one self; many souls resemble you, perhaps half of humanity resembles you, so how do you talk to people as if all of them were created like the creation of your self?! I am speaking of the ABC of reason and logic, and I am not speaking of the difficult and the deep in thought!

Allah the Exalted created humans, men and women, in diverse kinds, and you have reduced all of humanity to yourself and its particular creation, so where is your mind?!

As for the reason for the post, it is the boldness of those who speak on the pulpits when they do something that, by Allah, I feel terror when I reflect on it! When today I come out as a speaker and talk to people about issues with sensitive consequences within society, and I am not rightly guided, because memorising 10 thousand books does not mean guidance and never guarantees guidance, when I legislate for Islamic society today saying to its men: Whoever takes multiple wives in our time is mad; and before me is a man convinced by my words, and the word seizes him as one who trembles at imagined and exaggerated consequences is seized; this same man who attended my sermon, which was not right at the level of thought, his self is not like mine. For I am a speaker of fine eloquence in logic and wording, content by the ease of my make-up with one wife since I married 40 years ago, while the listener's make-up is other than mine, and his self was created wholly contrary to what my self was created upon. He trembles at my wrong theorising and is frightened by the word "mad", then his nature and make-up prod him, push him and drag him to their desires, so he goes to the forbidden. Whatever fatwa that was, it is either a fatwa of ignorance, and this is my opinion of the thinker who did not get it right, or a fatwa from betrayal to please the West among whom he was living, and this is not my opinion of him.""")

h(14, 2000, """Whoever gave a fatwa that it is disliked to practise an overpowering, compelling "halal of nature", due to the difficulty of fulfilling this halal in the most correct way in some age, has borne the sin of practising the forbidden outlets that whoever is convinced by his words will resort to!""")

t(14, 2495, """Were it not for Allah, our Mighty Lord, none of creation would be a thinker. Whatever means of building the mind the thinker has taken, they are means that dwindle greatly before the means taken by the cobbler, the servant in the house, the vegetable seller, the one who carries gas cylinders to the house, and others who serve society!""")

t(15, 95, """Thought has no high causal structure, because its beginning and foundation are a Divine selection and a great test, which is the test of the trust of the mind, and it is the costliest of the tests of the Hereafter; while the non-thinker has the means of causal structure available to a high degree in his abilities and his services to society, because he is not chosen for the test of the mind with its exorbitant cost, but is chosen only for the test of conduct, whose cost is not easy, but not as catastrophic as the cost of the test of the mind; because the trust of the mind means guidance or misguidance for groups, masses and humans, while the test of conduct is a test within the circle of family, relatives, friends, neighbours and the neighbourhood!

So which is more useful to the other?
The sound-minded thinker is useful to all people, but he gives people one thing, which is sound thought, while he takes from them hundreds of things of life! Can a thinker do without the services that people sell within society? The answer is no!

Can the non-thinker meet Allah the Exalted with a sound heart and his Lord pleased with him, without needing the thinker?
The answer is yes

So, O thinkers and owners of broad minds with good influence among people .. be humble before Allah the Mighty, our Lord, Whose names and attributes are sanctified, Who is magnified in the heavens and on earth, exalted be He with a great exaltation, and be humble among people.""")

h(15, 1000, """Let the thinker understand that those below him in thought and breadth of mind offer him far greater than what he offers them!”!""")

t(15, 1610, """When Jerusalem was under the control of the Crusaders, a Muslim from Jerusalem sent an eloquent and moving letter of appeal for help to Salah al-Din al-Ayyubi. These verses had a great effect on Salah al-Din's soul; the historical sources mention that he was strongly affected by them, and that they made him hasten to mobilise the armies and unite the ranks of the Muslims.

This poem was a fundamental moral motivation for Salah al-Din's efforts, until they were crowned with the conquest of Jerusalem and the liberation of al-Aqsa Mosque in the historic Battle of Hattin.""")

h(15, 2150, """O King who has turned upside down the emblems of the crosses, a complaint has come to you hastening from the Holy House: All the mosques have been purified, while I, despite my honour, am defiled""")

t(16, 180, """And what departs from the two norms is the testing of the obedient in moments of his humiliation despite his obedience, and the gradual leading-on of the sinner in moments of his rise despite his sin!""")

h(16, 600, """Obedience to Allah is authority on earth by heavenly mandate! And disobedience to Allah is humiliation on earth by heavenly command!""")

t(16, 1125, """Humanity, Muslims and non-Muslims, is living a real absurdity! A million books in the science of upbringing, and no upbringing!

The matter has become a show far from logic! For what are the million works on the science of upbringing?! What central thing has newly arisen in man psychologically and biologically?! Nothing. Everything new is the state of the usual logical, temporal and spatial changes in every historical cycle, and what the cycle calls for of human-human conflict on one hand, and conflict between man and his conscience on the other; then the historical cycle ends, the origin returns to its place, nature returns to its settled state, and man returns enlightened by 5 or 15 central ideas in upbringing. Then what will we do with the million books of muscle-flexing in theorising, and with the clear, certain failure in implementation, the failure society saw with its own eyes?! Most schools of upbringing deceive parents with crumbs of the promised change, and present themselves as the saviour from the globalisation of the twenty-first century; they are either private schools that did not understand the truth of what happened and is still happening, or private schools that understood and deceived families by presenting resounding slogans that cannot be implemented as they were portrayed. For the sake of this billion-dollar trade in the Islamic world, the names of private educational institutions were propped up with ornate intellectual facades, and those facades were evidenced by works "enormous" in number, by philosophical seminars and by courses that exaggerate in presenting inapplicable solutions, and the result is always zero in 99 of the generation! Enough.""")

h(16, 2050, """Exaggeration in displaying theories in a branch of the human sciences is not a healthy phenomenon!""")

t(17, 65, """What is within the capacity of one person's soul may be a fifth, a tenth or a quarter of what is within the capacity of another person, but that fifth, tenth or quarter represents for its owner his full hundred percent, so he says: My soul is filled with pains, and it truly is filled, not an illusion. If another is amazed and says to the afflicted: But there are those with greater pains and aches than you, that is a true statement, but the capacity of the afflicted one's soul is complete, because it has less capacity than the souls of those tested more severely than he was. So when a person cries out the cry of being full, he is, in most and the majority of cases, full, truly full!""")

h(17, 600, """Souls have a capacity, and every capacity in the soul is the highest limit of its patience!""")

h(17, 1500, """The one in error listens only to the strong. Understanding is settled!""")

t(17, 2050, """The humiliation of the older, poor in age, before the younger, well-off in age, in families, clans and homes. The voice of the knowers has grown hoarse in every time and place calling out among people: "This world tramples the dignity of those who glorify wealth, as a punishment for them, because the Mighty is Allah alone", but there is no life in the one you call .. For I have seen the young trample the dignity of one older than him, and the one whose dignity is trampled silent, mute, shaken, submissive like a servant; rather, with time he befriends and loves the one who tramples him!

This is the world that has pleased most people, that they loved and adored, and for which they spent the love of Allah and threw it behind their backs! This is how we see it doing to people .. making them very small while they think we do not see .. Yes, by Allah, we see very well with open eyes all the time, but we used to be silent with grief, rage and sorrow over the one who accepted being trampled; then, by Allah, we no longer ever grieve over one who has accepted contempt and humiliation for himself!""")
